# Accepted findings for the custody images. Each needs a reason and is re-examined when its dependency changes.
#
# CVE-2022-44797 (btcd before 0.23.2: BIP 68/112 consensus-rule bug). The signer takes btcd only through the threshold
# signing library, which imports github.com/btcsuite/btcd/btcec and nothing else of btcd's consensus code. Checked with
# `go list -deps ./...` in services/mpc-signer: the only btcd packages compiled in are btcec, chaincfg, chaincfg/chainhash
# and wire, none of which holds the affected consensus or script code. btcd cannot be raised to 0.23.2 because that
# release no longer ships the btcec package the library imports (go build fails).
CVE-2022-44797
